# Firebender Ascension counts a creature's attack causing a triggered ability *of that creature*. Ingris Stingerquill ("Whenever a creature
# you control attacks") is itself attacking alongside the Soldier token, so one attack-trigger of Ingris's is caused by the Soldier's attack
# and not by Ingris's own: the Soldier's firebending and Ingris's trigger for Ingris count, Ingris's trigger for the Soldier does not.
# Two quest counters, not three.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Firebender Ascension
Ingris Stingerquill
Mountain
Mountain x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Ingris Stingerquill.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Firebender Ascension.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Ingris Stingerquill; Soldier Token > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Firebender Ascension.Counters.Quest = 2

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Firebender Ascension.Counters.Quest = 2
